1940-The datum shapes and the reason vocabulary are unchanged by the move.
1941-
1942-When the DHT request interpreter resolves a name, it appends an
1943-admission question to an **admission request medium**. One interpreter
1944-reads the questions and appends answers to an **admission response
1945-medium**. The two ring media sit beside the link pair. The admission id
1946-is `[link-id serial]`. `serial` is a per-composition counter, never
1947-reused, so a retired question and a later question for the same link id
1948-never share an id.
1949-
1950-```clojure
1951-;; question, appended to the admission request medium at resolution
1952-{:yin.admit/id         [[:t0 7] 3]
1953- :yin.link/id          [:t0 7]
1954- :yin.admit/name       'pym.m
1955- :yin.admit/address    :segment/blake3-...   ; the resolved manifest address, retained
1956- :yin.admit/asserters  ["ed25519:<hex>" ...] ; every asserter of that entry (R8)
1957- :yin.admit/provenance {...}                 ; the entry's :yin.link/provenance verbatim
1958- :yin.link/format      f                     ; the request's own words, no subject
1959- :yin.link/contract    "b2"}
1960-
1961-;; answers, appended to the admission response medium
1962-{:yin.admit/id [[:t0 7] 3] :yin.admit/decision :allow  :yin.admit/conditions {}}
1963-{:yin.admit/id [[:t0 7] 3] :yin.admit/decision :refuse
1964- :yin.admit/reason :yin.admit/untrusted-principal :yin.admit/asserters [...]}
1965-```
