2045:#### 7.5.4 Parking, with no deadline, and retirement
2046-
2047-A link whose question is unanswered parks. The wait lives in the link
2048-pair's own protocol and adds no state: a parked link is a request the
2049-interpreter's request cursor has not passed, plus a retained question
2050-under `:asked`. Nothing lands on the link response medium until the
2051-answer does, so the VM's `:link` wait entry never learns admission
2052-exists. Nothing times the wait out: there is no clock in admission, and
2053-liveness belongs to `dao.lease` and to the `:link-policy` (8.3). An
2054-unanswered question ends only when an answer lands or its request is
2055-retired by abandonment.
2056-
2057-**Abandonment retires the run.** `mint-link-id` emits the current
2058-counter and then increments it, and child origins are minted the same way
2059-(origin `:t0.<n>` with `n` the current `:origins`). Both ranges are
2060-therefore half-open. `(abandon)` computes a run descriptor
2061-`{:origin :t0 :ids [from until] :children [from until]}` from `base`, the
2062-parked run's `(:base parked)`, and `parked`, the VM after the abandoned
2063-installs and links are folded out, with every counter normalized by
2064-`(or counter 0)`:
2065-
2066-- `:ids` is `[(:id-counter base) (:id-counter parked)]`.
2067-- `:children` is `[(:origins base) (:origins parked)]`.
2068-
2069-`(interpreter/retire {:pair :admission} run)` returns
2070-`{:pair :admission :retired [ids]}`. Walking the link pair's requests with
2071-`stream/next` from the pair's request cursor, a request with id `[o k]` is
2072-retired iff:
2073-
2074-- `o` is the run's origin and `base <= k < parked-counter`, that is
2075-  `from <= k < until` of `:ids`; or
2076-- for some `m` with `from <= m < until` of `:children`, with
2077-  `child = (str (name origin) "." m)`, `(name o)` equals `child` or starts
2078-  with `child + "."`, the exact origin or `origin + "."` of that child.
2079-
2080-A raw prefix never matches: `"t0.10"` does not start with `"t0.1."`, so
2081-`:t0.10` is never a descendant of `:t0.1`. Nested install children
2082-(`:t0.4.0`, `:t0.4.0.2`) match through the `"t0.4."` prefix. Each retired
2083-request advances the cursor. The first request that is not retired stops
2084-the walk, keeping serve's stop-at-first-unanswered rule, so a request
2085-outside the run is never skipped. Retire removes every `:asked` entry
2086-whose link id was retired and every `:answers` entry under those ids. No
2087-link response is appended for a retired request: the engine has already
2088-retired the id, and a response would be `:late`. An answer arriving later
2089-for a retired id correlates to nothing and the drain drops it.
2090-
2091-`:retired` names the run-owned requests the walk still encounters from the
2092-current cursor, before the first unrelated request. A root request that
2093-was already answered and spawned an install child is behind the cursor and
2094-is not in `:retired`; its child's requests are.
2095-
2096-`run-descriptor` and `retire` are the interpreter's; `(abandon)` is the
2097-REPL's command and, after AL-2, makes one `retire` call on the session's
2098-`:linker` value.
