2506-## 8. Evaluation
2507-
2508-### 8.1 Entry
2509-
2510-Loaded code enters a session by the flow of `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.2 and 7.3,
2511-unchanged: the require parks on the link pair; the interpreter answers under
2512-the request's id; the receiving task correlates, discharges obligations
2513-against its own live state (step 5b), runs the install child, and lowers its
2514-own bindings. This holds on all four VMs: each kernel names its format and
2515-contract through `IModuleKernel/link-format`, and the `:fallback` policy of
2516-`yin.vm.linker.md` 5.5 applies as composed.
2517-
2518-### 8.2 Pending and the re-check (R11)
2519-
2520-- A link the DHT source answers pending records, on the shell's pending
2521-  run, the module manifest address whose load it waits on.
2522-- `yin.repl.main/step-all` calls `yin.repl/recheck-pending` once in a tick
2523-  if and only if that tick's node events hold a `:loaded` or `:load-failed`
2524-  event whose `:manifest` is one a pending link waits on.
2525-- Any other node event (a bind, a publication settling, an index load,
2526-  another module's load) triggers no re-check and changes no `:checks`.
2527-- A terminal load event arrives once. A re-check after it finds the record
2528-  terminal and answers the link; a second re-check for the same address
2529-  cannot happen without a new load.
2530-- One re-check serves every pending request in order, so several pending
2531-  module loads completing in one tick need one re-check.
2532-- Beside it, `step-all` calls the AD-1 hook `yin.repl/recheck-on-answers`,
